\f0\fs24 \cf0 Bittersweet Ending:\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ending
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira stumbled into the room and her instincts kicked in faster than they ever had, she covered her face with her arm so none of the engineers could see who she was, and ran out of the room as fast as her legs could let her. Mira bolted out of the engine room and sprinting up the stairs, she could hear footsteps behind her and voices yelling, but she was faster.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira reached the school panting, she tried to catch her breath before entering the classroom, her hand clutching the buttons of her uniform as she looked at the portrait of president Veyr on the hall, staring into the eyes of a liar. She thought about going back home, but if the engineers decided to search the school and noticed her absence, they would most certainly realize it was her. So she took a deep breath and walked into the class.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 For the following three days Mira felt as if she was\'a0 being stalked, shadows that disappeared around the corner when she caught a glimpse of them, or sudden noises when she swore she was home alone. But then something much more shocking happened, it was third period, Mr. Marriott\'92s class, one of Mira\'92s most hated lessons, Governmental Structures. When there was a knock on the classroom door, Mr. Marriott allowed entry, and two members of the administration walked in, with Sara right in front of them.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira couldn\'92t believe her eyes, she could have bet all her money that Sara had been\'85removed by the government. She then thought she must have been dreaming, but looking at everyone\'92s reactions similar to her own, she realized just how real this was. Sara looked paler and thinner than when she had gone missing almost two weeks ago, something in her eyes even gave away her fear, and Mira noticed the bruising around her wrists and the faint red line around her neck that was almost entirely concealed by the uniform shirt.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Sara walked silently and sat down on the desk right next to Mira, never making eye contact with anyone. Right after the administration workers left, Sara slipped a note beneath their desks. Mira was almost shocked, Sara had always been an exemplary student, and slipping notes could get you publicly reprimanded and a disciplinary warning, she opened the small piece of paper carefully and looked at the words on them
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93They know you heard them\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira read the written message again and again, every single time her throat closed up further, her head pounded louder, her stomach turned, and a roll of nausea crept up her throat. All of what was left of the day she was unable to focus or socialize, every second felt like an hour. She walked home and locked herself in her room, unwilling to talk to anyone, not even her parents, once the the streets had quieted down, and her mother & father has retired to bed, she snuck out, walking up the staircase, if she used the elevators it would be recorded in the electricity usage reports.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 There were very few people roaming the silo at this hours, barely a couple more hours till curfew. Mira walked to Torin\'92s shop, completely empty except for the faint buzz of the fluorescents and Torin quite humming as he cleaned the tables, she walked in, made him sit down, and told him everything, the reports, her fear, sand finally Sara\'92s warning.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93You need to stop digging\'94 Torin said
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira looked at him, at his weary expression and the scar on his cheekbone
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93You knew. Didn\'92t you?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93I suspected\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira felt the anger rise in her chest, consuming her slowly
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93How did you find out?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93When I was doing maintenance once, I swam a bit further up than we are allowed to, and I saw some wonderful things Mira, vegetation covering entire buildings, birds flying in circles over us, do you know about birds? Read about them in school? If it truly was as radioactive as they said, no life could sustain up there\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Why didn\'92t you tell me?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Once they realized I knew, they threatened me Mira, the scar? It wasn\'92t a maintenance accident\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93But why would they do this?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93The first presidents weren\'92t lying, the bombs did happen, and there was radiation at first, but then it faded, and they started to relive just how well the silo worked, every person registered and every resource controlled, it was any politicians fantasy\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira looked at him and left without another word. The papers were leaked three days after, no one ever really found out who did it, some said Sara, others Mira, a few even speculated it had been Torin. The crash wasn\'92t sudden, it happened from the inside out, some believed the reports and claimed that they had always knew it was all a lie, meanwhile others claimed it was all a complex web of treason to defeat the government and that the outside was truly toxic.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 But the more people that started to question the reality they knew, the more unstable the Silo became. Schools were the first to shut down, then commerces, and ultimately all of the government administrated buildings, like the hospital. Everything was completely chaotic, strikes, riots even fights broke out through all the levels.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Then came the message of president Veyr, reproduced in every screen of the tank
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec2 \'93We did not continue the confinement of humanity out of cruelty,\'94 she said. \'93We continued it because history proved humanity destroys itself when given unlimited freedom.\'94
\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec2 Very few people felt any sort of comfort or honesty out of that broadcast, if anything it made the residents much more mistrustful with the government, so when some of the motors engineers warned of a flood in the lower level, no one evacuated or took shelter, they didn\'92t realise until half of the last level was completely underwater, so many died during the stampede of people escaping their homes, including Mrs. Rivers, and Sara who disappeared,\'a0 would truly never be seen again.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 After the floods a group the resistance, leaded by Mira had Torin fought until they were allowed to leave to the surface, promising to never return to the Silo, and they all agreed. A few rising platforms were displayed in the highest level of the tank, the one only accessible to the president and their families, Mira had never seen or felt as much sunlight as she could now through the transparent ceiling, she and Torin stepped into the center one, and many others to the ones surrounding them.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira looked around, and in the group of people who had chosen to stay in the tank she saw Ocean, she warned Torin and ran off, sprinting to her
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Ocean! Come on, there\'92s still a few spots left in the platforms\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93No, Mira I\'92m staying behind\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93What? How can you do this? After everything we\'92ve discovered?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93The lie was evil, but it was also necessary to keep us safe Mira, to keep control\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Ocean please, you can\'92t imagine how beautiful it is up there\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Good luck Mira, I wish I was half as brave as you\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Please\'85\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira would have continued trying to convince her for hours, if it hadn't been for Torin yelling out her name, signalling that the platforms were about to ascend, Mira looked one more time at Ocean, and ran back to Torin, who helped her up.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 The ride up was almost impossible to handle, feeling the hair in her arms stand up, shielding her eye the higher up they went, feeling the warmth of the sun on her skin, and hearing the waves crash against the shore, the platforms floated ashore, and the opening they had left through, the lights of the silo dim underwater. But Mira couldn\'92t focus on that, she saw the massive buildings covered in green vegetation and the birds flying in flock over them just like Torin had described.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She then looked at the people around them, all that had lost, all they had risked, for freedom, even if it meant they would live in uncertainty for the rest of their time.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93They\'92ll rebuild down there\'94 Torin said looking at her
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93And we\'92ll rebuild up here\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 The end.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
}